    "body": "@domenic is it cool to tweak the html as well? To @Munter's point, if you're willing to contain the non-number content in a new element (span or what have you) so you always have 2 spans as the children of the `a`, then the flex behavior is much cleaner, letting you e.g. have your content in a block and not wrap under the number.  You could also then independently influence underline for the content as compared to the numbers.\r\n\r\nFor example see this quick fiddle: https://jsfiddle.net/6v1as46z/",
